    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "First, look toward the Sun. Closest to it is little Mercury, its surface marked by many",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.515,
        675.865,
        626.9549999999998,
        691.51
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "impact craters. Next comes Venus, wrapped in a thick atmosphere. Although it is farther",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.17,
        697.865,
        659.2950000000001,
        713.75
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "from the Sun, its powerful greenhouse effect makes it hotter than Mercury. It is the",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
